*.pyc
.DS_Store

# NER expansion (scripts/16-21): raw/processed geospatial rasters and large
# OSM road pulls are regeneratable via those scripts (deterministic, given
# cached source downloads) -- not committing them. Several already exceed
# GitHub's 100MB hard push limit (Assam/Arunachal Pradesh's processed DEM,
# slope, aspect and LS-factor rasters run 300-370MB each), and the full set
# is ~9GB total. The small, irreplaceable deliverables -- landslide CSVs,
# boundary vectors, negative samples, rainfall points, and the final
# training_dataset_<state>.csv files -- are NOT covered by these rules and
# stay tracked normally. Regenerate anything excluded here by re-running
# scripts/18_run_state_pipeline.py / 19 / 20 / 21 for the state in question.
data/raw/Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_*.tif
data/raw/ESA_WorldCover_10m_2021_v200_*.tif
data/raw/soil_*_0-5cm.tif
data/processed/*.tif
data/raw/*_roads.geojson
data/interim/
